given-names></name><name><surname>McGee</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Sharma</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><source>The Injury Chart Book: A graphical overview of the global burden of injuries</source><year>2002</year><publisher-name>Geneva: World Health Organization</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Krug</surname><given-names>EG</given-names></name><name><surname>Dahlberg</surname><given-names>LL</given-names></name><name><surname>Mercy</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Zwi</surname><given-names>AB</given-names></name><name><surname>Lozano</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><source>World Report on Violence and Health</source><year>2003</year><publisher-name>Geneva: World Health Organization</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Uauy</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Albala</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Kain</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Obesity trends in Latin America: transiting from under- to overweight</article-title><source>J Nutr</source><year>2001</year><volume>131</volume><fpage>893S</fpage><lpage>899S</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11238781</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Monteiro</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Conde</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Popkin</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Obesity and inequities in health in the developing world</article-title><source>International Journal of Obesity</source><year>2004</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>1181</fpage><lpage>1